A||||4||mrfixit58||Someone was looking out for me (or maybe my 87 GT)||||6||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||06-04-2001||05:20 PM||||Well, Last Thursday morning I got up and headed out the door like usual and jumped into my 87 GT. I started her up and tried to back her out of the garage and almost stalled the motor. On the second try, the same results. It was only then that I realized something seemed different about how the car was sitting. Turned out, it was a flat left rear tire. I had walked right by it and didn't notice until I tried to back out.<P>Annoyed, I aired the tire and moved it out of the way so I could get my truck out and then put the 87 back into the garage to fix later and proceeded to work kinda bummed.<P>Fast forward to 5:00 pm... I'm on the way home and approaching the usual back up. I'm in the right lane heading east (one of three) and moving up to the light when out of NO WHERE, a C1500 pulls right out in front of me and WHAM! POW! the air bag goes off.<P>Seems two very polite truck drivers decided to leave a gap for a guy to cross the road. The trucks that they were driving were too big for either me to see him or him to see me. He, being young and trusting, pulled out into my lane without being able to see if it was clear.<P>Good new is, no one was seriously hurt. Bad news, my truck suffered about $4,000 damage. Good news, I wasn't driving my 87 GT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Moral of the story... if you can't see, don't go! AND IF you can't drive your favorite Fiero for some reason, it may be a good thing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Urchin||06-04-2001||05:25 PM||||wow, I've had a few near misses in similar situations.  Glad to hear you only have to fix a flat rather than a possible write off.  Sorry 'bout the truck though, glad everyone was ok<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_3.jpg">   <P>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||06-04-2001||05:38 PM||||Nearly the same thing happend to my wife one day while coming to pick me up from work. She was approaching a wide single lane intersection and a SUV  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> was making a left. Well the person in the oncoming lane was making a left also and without being able to see around a 5 story building of an SUV just went ahead like an idiot made the left without seeing if it was clear. WHAMO! According to my wife the other car lept up and over the hood of my car and did a 180. and backed into a fence. Totaled both cars. My passanger door gets jammed and wont close, and the windshield is soooooo close to stress cracking that it's begining to delaminate.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Pictures/image006.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000003||sqoach||06-04-2001||05:42 PM||||Glad to hear everyone is ok.<P>84Bill, that almost looks like blood on your car! I'm sure it got some stares from that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||06-04-2001||10:38 PM||||LOL yeah come to think of it not to many people decided to pull out in front of me after that.||||reg||10
